{
  "metadata": {
    "projectName": "Predictive Analytics in Digital Twin Systems: A Systematic Literature Review of Architectures, Algorithms, and Technical Challenges",
    "researchQuestions": "RQ 1. What are the predictive analytic approaches in a digital twin-based system?\n\nRQ1.1: What are the primary domains, operational scales, and maturity levels of current predictive Digital Twins?\n\nRQ1.2: What system architectures, data pipelines, and cyber-physical interfaces are utilized to support predictive analytics?\n\nRQ1.3: Which predictive algorithms form the analytic core, and how are their performances validated?\n\nRQ1.4: What are the recognized technical limitations and architectural challenges in deploying these predictive systems?",
    "inclusionCriteria": "All that passes the EC.",
    "exclusionCriteria": "Exclusion rule: Boolean OR; if any single criterion is met, the paper is strictly EXCLUDED. The sequence is optimized for a fail-fast mechanism.\n\nEC1 (Wrong Document Type): The document is explicitly classified as a secondary or non-peer-reviewed source, such as a Review, Survey, Bibliometric study, Book chapter, or Conference summary lacking a full-text architectural proposition.\n\nEC2 (Absence of System Context): The abstract completely fails to mention a physical asset context, a cyber-physical system (CPS), or a system-level architecture. It operates purely in an isolated virtual space without acknowledging hardware or integration topologies.\n\nEC3 (Absence of Predictive Analytics): The abstract details passive logging systems, condition monitoring, 3D visualizations (CAD/BIM), or basic rule-based control without implementing AI/ML forecasting or future-state predictive modeling.\n\nEC4 (Pure Algorithmic Benchmarking): The experiments explicitly focus 100% on pure algorithmic or mathematical performance benchmarking (e.g., isolated model accuracy metrics on static datasets) WITHOUT proposing, evaluating, or explicitly discussing how the model is integrated into a system architecture, framework, or edge-cloud topology. (Note: The use of simulation or synthetic data is NOT an automatic disqualifier if an architecture is being evaluated).\n\nEC5 (Failed 3-Pillar Architectural Integration): The full text fails to comprehensively describe a complete or conceptually sound Digital Twin framework. It must explicitly detail: (1) a physical or cyber-physical context, (2) a predictive computational core, and (3) a system integration mechanism (data pipelines, architectural topology). Crucial Distinction: Papers proposing reference architectures or distributed topologies validated via simulation tools (e.g., CloudSim, edge-emulators) are INCLUDED. Papers using simulation solely to test algorithmic accuracy without defining an underlying system architecture are EXCLUDED.\n\nEC6 (Static Rule-Based Systems): The described control or decision-making system relies entirely on static, hard-coded threshold rules (e.g., simple \"if-then\" logic for temperature control) without employing data-driven predictive algorithms.\n\nEC7 (Accessibility & Formatting): The full text is not available in English, is hidden behind inaccessible paywalls (unresolvable via institutional access), or possesses corrupted document formatting preventing programmatic or human extraction.\n\nEC8 (Critical Failure): In The Scientist phase, the full text is triggered at least one of the critical QA.\n\nEC9 (Low Score Threshold): In The Scientist phase, the full text total score is below 4.5.",
