    {
      "Paper_ID": "Chen_2025_Fatiguecrackpre_a1008",
      "Year": 2025,
      "Title": "Fatigue crack prediction based on distributed optical fiber sensing data and dynamic Bayesian network",
      "Authors": "Chen, Shuai (58954536100); Xu, Hao (56576514600); Zhao, Shiyuan (57189387680); Tan, Deyang (59934603900); Dong, Zimai (59934967800); Qu, Xiaoxi (57188719756); Yang, Lei (56883267200); Wu, Zhanjun (8696478900)",
      "Abstract": "Fatigue crack propagation critically endangers aircraft structural integrity. Traditional digital twin (DT) combines dynamic Bayesian networks (DBNs) with offline non-destructive evaluation (NDE) data for crack prognosis, but reliance on periodic inspections causes delayed parameter updates and prediction uncertainties. This study proposes an online monitoring framework using optical frequency domain reflectometry (OFDR) strain data to enhance crack prediction. To ensure the acquisition of high-resolution, reliable fiber sensing data, we introduce a hybrid moving window algorithm coupled with measurement optimization protocols for OFDR-based distributed strain measurements. Additionally, a sliding window principal component analysis (SW-PCA) methodology is proposed to enable precise crack length quantification and spatial localization. Furthermore, we advance the DBN framework by integrating an enhanced particle filtering (PF) algorithm to dynamically model crack propagation trajectories and estimate residual structural life with improved fidelity. The proposed methodology was validated through controlled fatigue crack propagation experiments on compact tension specimens. Comparative analyses revealed that the online monitoring-driven approach achieved superior predictive accuracy and significantly reduced dispersion in prognostic results relative to conventional offline NDE-based predictions. These findings underscore the transformative potential of the developed framework for enhancing the robustness and practical applicability of DT systems in aerospace structural health management. © 2025 Elsevier Ltd",
      "DOI_Link": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.measurement.2025.118070",
      "Link": "https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105007511220&doi=10.1016%2Fj.measurement.2025.118070&partnerID=40&md5=20628affd3f2867dfe63c0a89706217a",
      "Publisher": "Elsevier B.V.",
      "DOI": "10.1016/j.measurement.2025.118070",
      "Conference name": "",
      "Source": "scopus_09-04-2026",
      "Thinking_Token_Abstract_Screening": 651,
