    {
      "Paper_ID": "Reddy_2025_Deeplearningbas_b7909",
      "Year": 2025,
      "Title": "Deep learning based optical metrology for real-time sensing: Optical flow estimation",
      "Authors": "Reddy, Yuvarajendra Anjaneya (59112560800); Sjödahl, Mikael (7003761457)",
      "Abstract": "Advancements in deep learning have significantly broadened the scope of optical metrology, enabling real-time, high-precision sensing for industrial and environmental applications. This work investigates the integration of deep learning with optical flow estimation-specifically in particle image velocimetry (PIV), a non-intrusive flow visualization technique-to improve accuracy, computational efficiency, and adaptability. We introduce end-to-end models that reliably estimate dense flow fields from consecutive time-resolved particle images, optimized for resource-constrained environments. By utilizing core neural network operations such as automatic differentiation and backpropagation, the models extract higher-order flow moments, which are incorporated into training implicitly via physics-informed loss functions or explicitly as evaluation metrics. This hybrid strategy ensures physically consistent and interpretable predictions. Beyond PIV, the framework is adaptable to a wide range of optical metrology methods, offering a scalable solution across multiple domains. Its real-time capabilities position it as a valuable tool within digital twin frameworks, enabling predictive maintenance, adaptive control, and sustainable manufacturing through process optimization and surface quality assessment. By combining data-driven learning with governing physics, this approach bridges fluid dynamics, environmental monitoring, and advanced manufacturing-fostering interdisciplinary collaboration and enabling efficient, informed decision-making. © 2025 SPIE. All rights reserved.",
      "DOI_Link": "https://doi.org/10.1117/12.3062529",
      "Link": "https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105026961924&doi=10.1117%2F12.3062529&partnerID=40&md5=5481c6973695156a6651517eb18b8c10",
      "Publisher": "SPIE",
      "DOI": "10.1117/12.3062529",
      "Conference name": "Multimodal Sensing and Artificial Intelligence for Sustainable Future",
      "Source": "scopus_09-04-2026",
      "Thinking_Token_Abstract_Screening": 2786,
      "Candidate_Token_Abstract_Screening": 231,
      "Input_Token_Abstract_Screening": 1353,
      "Total_Token_Abstract_Screening": 4370
    },
    {
      "Paper_ID": "Singh_2025_AIDrivenPredict_7a38f",
      "Year": 2025,
      "Title": "AI-Driven Predictive Analytics for Secure IoT-Enabled Smart Agriculture and Public Administration Perspectives",
      "Authors": "Singh, Harshita (60215774000); Bari, Sudhriti (60215774100); Singh, Sushil Kumar (57211843264); Suthar, Om Prakash (58478837800)",
      "Abstract": "This chapter explores how AI and predictive analytics, as well as advanced nextgen technologies, are transforming traditional agriculture into smart farming with IoT technologies in the Smart City Environment. Integration of IoT devices, AI, blockchain, drones, 6G networks, edge computing, and digital twins enables realtime monitoring of various agricultural activities. AI-backed predictive models help in forecasting irrigation needs, identifying early crop health monitoring, and optimizing resource usage. Blockchain and smart contracts help in ensuring data security and transparency. However, challenges include cybersecurity risks, limited rural connectivity, and the need for improved digital literacy is evident. The chapter discusses and highlights both advancements in technology and the role of policy, governance, and digital inclusion in achieving secure and efficient smart agriculture. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.",
      "DOI_Link": "https://doi.org/10.4018/979-8-3373-3760-9.ch002",
      "Link": "https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105023263347&doi=10.4018%2F979-8-3373-3760-9.ch002&partnerID=40&md5=9a92d05e9ebc28fe93a5cd2699efee91",
      "Publisher": "IGI Global",
